<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- shiroikuma-termux: the 白い熊 Termux UI page — a folding accordion under a chip index.

     Top to bottom: 「App settings ›」 (the thick pill to Termux's own settings; not a section), the
     chip index (added in code: ShiroikumaIndexPreference, one chip per section), then the
     sections. A section is a ShiroikumaSectionCategory with key `section_<id>`; its icon and its
     section-icon colour come from the registry in ShiroikumaUiFragment (SECTIONS), which heading
     and chip both read. THE ORDER BELOW IS THE DEFAULT ORDER: App language first, and no two
     neighbours of one section colour. The order the page shows is the stored one
     (ShiroikumaPageState), every section folded by default.

     Rows: ShiroikumaActionPreference = an outlined pill (opens / runs something); a plain
     ShiroikumaPreference / SwitchPreferenceCompat / ShiroikumaSeekBarPreference = a control row;
     a ShiroikumaPreference with the subheader layout = a sub-heading, rows under it take the
     indent2 / seekbar_l2 layouts. No layout carries a colour — ShiroikumaRows draws every row from
     the page's roles. Nothing here persists on its own (persistent="false" everywhere):
     ShiroikumaUiFragment wires every row by key to ShiroikumaTheme (prefs file `shiroikuma_ui`),
     to the device-local automation / external-apps files or to the terminal files under ~/.termux,
     and every change previews live. -->
